i. {A, D}, {A, E}, {B, D}, {C, F}
ii. {A, B}, {B, C}, {A, D}, {D, F}
b. What is cardinality of min-cut in this graph?
c. Prove that if a connected undirected graph with $n$ vertices has a min-cut of cardinality $k$, then $G$ has at least $nk/2$ edges.
